cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "BitNet RL: GRPO for the missing reinforcement-learning stage of 1.58-bit LLMs"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Poorgholam
    given-names: Ahmad
version: "1.1"
date-released: 2026-10-07
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/ahmadpoorgholam/bitnet-rl"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch PyTorch implementation of Group Relative Policy Optimization (GRPO)
  for the reinforcement-learning stage that the BitNet b1.58 training recipe leaves
  as future work, with an independent NumPy reference, a BitLinear policy, and
  CPU-only validation at toy scale. No real BitNet checkpoint has been trained.
keywords:
  - BitNet
  - 1.58-bit LLM
  - ternary weights
  - quantization-aware training
  - reinforcement learning
  - GRPO
  - DeepSeek-R1
  - RLVR
  - policy gradient
  - reasoning
  - PyTorch
  - NumPy
